// Generated from content/help/*.mdx by lib/help/generate.ts. Do not edit.
export const HELP_SOURCES: Readonly<Record<string, string>> = {
  "briefs": "---\ntitle: Brief sheets\ntags: briefs,hearing-prep,summary\nsurface: briefs\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nA brief sheet is a one-page summary of a listing, prepared before the hearing.\n\n## What it holds\n\n- The matter, court, hall and item number.\n- The last order and the next date.\n- Open obligations and your notes.\n\n## Using it\n\nOpen **Briefs** to see sheets for upcoming listings. Print a sheet or open it on your phone in court. Sheets are rebuilt when the matter changes.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "capture-inbox": "---\ntitle: The capture inbox\ntags: capture,inbox,voice,camera\nsurface: inbox\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nEverything that arrives lands in the Inbox as a capture.\n\n## Statuses\n\n- **Processing**: being read.\n- **Needs you**: a decision is required.\n- **Ready**: waiting to be applied.\n\n## Channels\n\nEmail, voice notes, camera photos, WhatsApp and calendar files each have their own opt-in under **Settings, Channels**. You can discard or pin any capture.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "clerk-role-limits": "---\ntitle: Clerk role limits\ntags: clerk,roles,members,permissions\nsurface: general\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nA clerk can prepare work but cannot change who has access.\n\n## What a clerk can do\n\n- View matters they are given and prepare captures and briefs.\n- Propose changes that an advocate accepts.\n\n## What a clerk cannot do\n\n- Invite or remove members, or change roles.\n- Export or delete the workspace.\n- See sensitive matters unless an advocate includes them.\n\nOwners manage roles from **Settings, Members**.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "export-and-delete": "---\ntitle: Export and delete your data\ntags: export,delete,lifecycle,data\nsurface: general\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nYou can take your data out or remove it.\n\n## Export\n\nOwners can request a full export from **Settings, Data**. The export is prepared in the background and a download link is sent when ready.\n\n## Delete\n\nDeleting the workspace starts a grace period during which you can cancel. After it ends, the workspace and its files are erased.\n\nBoth actions are recorded in the audit log and need a recent two-factor check.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "first-court-day-view": "---\ntitle: Your first court-day view\ntags: court-day,today,hearings,getting-started\nsurface: today\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nThe Court-Day Board is the page you open each morning. It lists today's hearings grouped by court and hall, so you can see where you need to be and in what order.\n\n## Reading the board\n\n- Each row is one listing: matter, court, hall and the item number.\n- Live halls show the item now being heard and an estimate of when your item will be reached.\n- Bench notices that affect your matters appear above the list.\n\n## If the board is empty\n\nForward a cause list to your intake address or import one from **Inbox**. Hearings appear here as soon as the list is read.\n\nSee also [importing lists and orders](importing-lists-and-orders).\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "forwarding-cause-lists": "---\ntitle: Forwarding cause lists by email\ntags: email,intake,allow-list,cause-list\nsurface: inbox\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nEvery member has a private intake address.\n\n## Set up\n\n- Create the address in **Settings, Email intake**.\n- Add the senders you trust to the allow-list.\n- Forward a cause list or order to the address.\n\nMail from other senders is ignored. Rotate or revoke the address at any time.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "importing-lists-and-orders": "---\ntitle: Importing lists and orders\ntags: import,cause-list,orders,inbox\nsurface: inbox\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nYou can bring cause lists and orders into CauseDeck by forwarding them, uploading files or importing a batch.\n\n## Ways in\n\n- **Forward by email** to your private intake address. Only senders on your allow-list are read.\n- **Upload files** from Capture. PDFs and photos are read on the server.\n- **Bulk import** a folder of past lists to build your matters.\n\n## What happens next\n\nEvery file becomes a capture in your Inbox. Nothing changes your matters until you accept the proposals it produces. See [proposals and undo](proposals-and-undo).\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "keyboard-shortcuts": "---\ntitle: Keyboard shortcuts\ntags: shortcuts,keyboard,navigation\nsurface: general\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nPress **?** anywhere outside a text field to open the shortcut sheet.\n\n## Common keys\n\n- **c** opens capture.\n- **g then t** goes to Today.\n- **/** focuses the page search.\n- **mod+k** opens the command palette.\n\nOn touch devices the sheet is replaced by a short gestures guide.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "memory-review": "---\ntitle: Reviewing memory\ntags: memory,review,confirm\nsurface: memory\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nMemory is what the workspace has learned about your matters, such as a judge's usual directions or how a client is addressed.\n\n## Review\n\n- New items wait for your confirmation before they are used.\n- Confirm, edit or remove any item.\n- Removed items are not suggested again.\n\n## Scope\n\nMemory belongs to your workspace. It is never shared with other workspaces.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "notifications": "---\ntitle: Notifications and quiet hours\ntags: notifications,email,alerts\nsurface: general\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nCauseDeck can alert you about hearings, notices and obligations.\n\n## Choosing what to receive\n\nOpen **Settings, Notifications** to pick channels and categories. Quiet hours hold non-urgent alerts until the morning.\n\nThe bell opens the latest alerts; press **shift+n** to open it from the keyboard.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "obligations": "---\ntitle: Obligations and the queue\ntags: obligations,directions,due-dates\nsurface: obligations\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nDirections and undertakings recorded in orders become obligations with a due date.\n\n## The queue\n\n- Overdue items are listed first, then those due soon.\n- Each obligation links to the order line it came from.\n- Mark an obligation done, or move it with a reason.\n\n## Adding your own\n\nUse **New obligation** on a matter to record something that was agreed in court but is not in an order.\n\nDue dates are computed in Indian Standard Time.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "offline-mode": "---\ntitle: Working offline\ntags: offline,pwa,connectivity\nsurface: general\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nCauseDeck keeps working when the connection drops.\n\n## What works offline\n\n- Today's board and your recent matters.\n- Help articles, including this one.\n- Captures you make are queued and sent when you are back online.\n\n## What needs a connection\n\nImports, support requests and anything that reads a court website.\n\nA banner tells you when you are offline and when queued items have been sent.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "privacy-and-india-only-ai": "---\ntitle: Privacy and India-only AI\ntags: privacy,ai,data-residency\nsurface: general\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nYour data stays in India.\n\n## AI processing\n\n- AI features run only on providers in India.\n- Sensitive matters are never sent to AI.\n- Each AI result shows its source so you can check it.\n\n## Access to your workspace\n\nStaff see no case content by default. A support session shows only metadata, lasts for the time you choose, and is recorded in the audit log.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "proposals-and-undo": "---\ntitle: Proposals and undo\ntags: proposals,undo,automation,activity\nsurface: inbox\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nCauseDeck suggests changes as proposals instead of editing your matters silently.\n\n## Proposals\n\n- A proposal shows what would change and the source line it came from.\n- Accept it, edit it, or dismiss it.\n- Items that need a person go to **Needs you** in the Inbox.\n\n## Undo\n\nEvery applied change is recorded in Activity. Open the entry and choose **Undo** to reverse it, together with anything that was applied in the same step.\n\nUndo is available for a limited time after an import; the Activity entry shows the deadline.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "reading-the-court-day-board": "---\ntitle: Reading live hall status\ntags: court-day,live,halls,bench-notices\nsurface: today\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nLive hall status shows which item a hall is hearing now.\n\n## How to read it\n\n- **Item now** is the listing currently called.\n- **N away** counts the items between that one and yours.\n- The estimated window is a guide based on recent pace, not a promise.\n\nStatus comes from the court's public display and may lag behind the room.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
  "requesting-support": "---\ntitle: Getting support\ntags: support,whatsapp,contact\nsurface: general\nupdated: 2026-10-25\n---\n\nOpen the Contact tab in Help to reach us.\n\n## Options\n\n- Chat on WhatsApp during court-day hours.\n- Email us when WhatsApp is not available.\n- Owners can **Request a support session**.\n\nA support session is time-boxed, shows staff metadata only and ends automatically. You can end it earlier from **Settings, Support**.\n\nThis is software documentation, not legal advice.\n",
};
